Subject: gdbsupport eintr.h: retry open() without the handle_eintr template

Why: bionic declares ::open with FORTIFY overloads, so clang cannot deduce the function template argument of
gdb::handle_eintr (-1, ::open, ...) and gdbsupport does not compile.
Source: termux-packages packages/gdb/gdbsupport-eintr.h.patch at commit eb1c6b3abce4979882df8d61328f0124e44adbe4, with the file names in the
diff header changed to a/ b/.

--- a/gdbsupport/eintr.h
+++ b/gdbsupport/eintr.h
@@ -82,7 +82,12 @@
 inline int
 open (const char *pathname, int flags)
 {
-  return gdb::handle_eintr (-1, ::open, pathname, flags);
+  ssize_t ret;
+  do {
+      errno = 0;
+      ret = ::open(pathname, flags);
+  } while (ret == -1 && errno == EINTR);
+  return ret;
 }
 
 #ifdef HAVE_WAIT
